{{also|Grenade}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From French {{term|grenade|lang=fr}}, from Old French {{term|grenate|lang=fro}} in the phrase {{term|pome grenate||pomegranate|lang=fro}}, ultimately from Latin {{term|pomum granatum||seeded fruit|lang=la}}. The ''-d'' developed in French under influence of Spanish {{term|granada|lang=es}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɡɹəˈneɪd/}}
*: {{rhymes|eɪd}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{obsolete}} A [[pomegranate]].
# A small [[explosive]] [[device]], designed to be thrown by hand or launched from a grenade launcher.

====Derived terms====
* [[grenadier]]
* [[grenadine]]
* [[grenade launcher]]
* [[hand grenade]]
* [[grenadelike]]

